// A const's type is Int, Decimal, String or Bool, and that shortlist is not arbitrary: a const
// IS a literal with a name, so a type with no literal form has nothing a const could hold.
//
// One rule covers CInt, CDouble, CPointer, arrays, classes and enums at once, which is better
// for a reader than meeting six separate refusals and having to work out what they share. A
// CInt in particular arrives from a marshaller at an `external function` boundary — there is
// no way to write one down.
const WIDTH: CInt = 1;
print(1);
